preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >
    Computational Methods for Data Augmentation and Labeling in Oriented
    Object Detection from Remote Sensing Imagery: A Critical Review of
    Algorithms, Documented Failures, and Engineering Guidelines
  authors:
    - family-names: Madaan
      given-names: Nishi
    - family-names: Malik
      given-names: Rahul
  journal: "Applied Intelligence"
  publisher:
    name: Springer
  year: 2025
  status: "under-review"
  abstract: >
    We present a PRISMA-compliant systematic review of 112 peer-reviewed
    works spanning 2014-2025, synthesised through a DerSimonian-Laird
    random-effects meta-analysis of 387 effect-size observations
    (I^2=73.4%, mean mAP gain +6.9%, 95% CI: 5.8-8.0%). Four previously
    undocumented field-wide failures are reported: a 59% OBB rotation
    implementation error rate, the GAN Paradox (r=-0.89, p<0.001), the
    Benchmark Overfitting Index (BOI), and five cardinal evaluation failures
    inflating reported gains by 1.2-16x.
